    "text": "E3 said: the cheapest way to give a small model reasoning is often not to run RL on it, but to **copy a strong teacher's homework**: let the teacher write out its solutions, keep only the right ones, and fine-tune on them. DeepSeek found that at 32B, a model distilled this way beat the same model trained with large-scale RL[^r1-en]."
